  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 15 January 1932; five candidates were nominated for four seats, but one withdrew and four were returned unopposed (Mid-Ulster Mail, 9 January 1932, p. 5). 'UNIONIST CANDIDATES RETURNED UNOPPOSED.' Five nominations were lodged: Joseph I. Thompson, John Glasgow, William Alexander, J. D. Hopper and Hamilton Clements (Labour Unionist). 'Mr. Hopper's nomination was withdrawn' on grounds of economy, and the other four were returned. The three Unionists and one Labour Unionist are elected unopposed; the paper gives no votes. Returned unopposed."
